Algorithm 2: Resource Management

Input:
Owner o, Admin a, Supplier wallet w, Provider ID i, Resource type R, Quantity q, Flag fl, Timestamp t

Output:
Resource updated, compliance status returned, or transaction reverted with an appropriate error.

Pseudocode
Algorithm 2: Resource Management

1.  if msg.sender == a OR
        msg.sender == o OR
        msg.sender == allowedContract then

2.      Open or close resource form

3.  else
4.      Reject transaction
5.      Error: "Unauthorized"


6.  if Supplier is registered AND
        Resource form is open then

7.      Fetch Provider ID i

8.      Validate resource type R and quantity q

9.      if Resource type R or quantity q is invalid then
10.         Reject transaction
11.         Error: "Invalid resource or quantity"

12.     Store or update resource information:
        <R, q, t, fl>

13.     Emit ResourceQuantityUpdated event

14. else
15.     Reject transaction
16.     Error: "Invalid state"


17. if Compliance check is requested then

18.     Fetch the timestamp of the last resource update

19.     Calculate:
        Current timestamp - Last update timestamp

20.     if Last update <= 7 days then
21.         Return COMPLIANT

22.     else
23.         Return NON-COMPLIANT
